<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63805" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοιβ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λείβω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pouring.</i> only in religious sense,
			<i>drink-offering</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοιβῇ τε κνίσῃ
			τε</span> with <i>drink-offering</i> and burnt-offering, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.500
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.70
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοὶ δ᾽ αὖ λ. φέρον</span> says
			Odysseus to the Cyclops, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.349
			</span></i>: later, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδαί, χοαί</span>
			 (which are more freq.), in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				11.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				52
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοιβαὶ Διός</span>, offered to
			him, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				55
			</span></i>. -- Rare in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. οἴνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					906d
				</span></i>
			, referring to <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.500
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of
			<i>water</i> generally, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. Στυγός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.291
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
